artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let G = (V(G), E(G)) be a finite simple undirected graph. For a positive integer m, G is called m-connected if |V(G)| > m and G remains connected after the removal of any set of fewer than m vertices. For S ⊆ V(G), G[S] denotes the subgraph induced by S, and a partition (S, T) of V(G) means S ∪ T = V(G), S ∩ T = ∅, with both S and T nonempty.

Prove or disprove: For every positive integer ℓ, there exists a positive integer k = k(ℓ) such that for every k-connected graph G and every subset X ⊆ V(G) with |X| ≤ ℓ, there is a partition (S, T) of V(G) satisfying all of the following:
  (i) X ⊆ S;
  (ii) every vertex of S has at least ℓ neighbors in T;
  (iii) the induced subgraph G[S] is ℓ-connected;
  (iv) the induced subgraph G[T] is ℓ-connected.

